<article class="env-lemma" id="0A3T">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A3T">Lemma <span data-tag="0A3T">59.91.4</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a proper morphism of schemes. Let $\overline{s} \to S$ be a geometric point. For any sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$ the canonical map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (f_*\mathcal{F})_{\overline{s}} \longrightarrow \Gamma (X_{\overline{s}}, \mathcal{F}_{\overline{s}})  \]
</div>
  <p> is bijective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Theorem <a href="/tag/03Q9" data-tag="03Q9">59.53.1</a> (for sheaves of sets) we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  (f_*\mathcal{F})_{\overline{s}} = \Gamma (X \times _ S \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}_{S, \overline{s}}^{sh}), p_{small}^{-1}\mathcal{F})  \]
</div>
    <p>
       where $p : X \times _ S \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}_{S, \overline{s}}^{sh}) \to X$ is the projection. Since the residue field of the strictly henselian local ring $\mathcal{O}_{S, \overline{s}}^{sh}$ is $\kappa (s)^{sep}$ we conclude from the discussion above the lemma and Lemma <a href="/tag/0A3S" data-tag="0A3S">59.91.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>